/-!
# The inverse image of a power of an ideal sheaf is a quotient of the pullback

Let `h : Z ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes and let `I` be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on `X`.
The inverse image ideal sheaf `h⁻¹I` is generated by the image of `I`, so for every `n` the
pullback of `Iⁿ` as a sheaf of modules surjects onto `(h⁻¹I)ⁿ`:

`h^*(Iⁿ) ⟶ (h⁻¹I)ⁿ`.

Together with the multiplication epimorphism
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealProduct.epi_idealPowMulOfHom` this produces the epimorphism

`pr₁^*(𝓘ⁿ) ⊗ pr₂^*(𝓘'ⁿ) ⟶ 𝓙ⁿ`, `𝓙 = pr₁^*𝓘 · pr₂^*𝓘'`

onto a power of the product ideal sheaf of a fibre product.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.pushforwardSubmodule`: the pushforward of a subsheaf
  of a sheaf of modules, as a subsheaf of the pushforward.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.idealPowToPushforward`: the adjoint transpose
  `Iⁿ ⟶ h_*((h⁻¹I)ⁿ)` of the morphism below.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.pullbackIdealPow`: the morphism
  `h^*(Iⁿ) ⟶ (h⁻¹I)ⁿ`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.externalTensorIdealPowMul`: the morphism
  `pr₁^*(𝓘ⁿ) ⊗ pr₂^*(𝓘'ⁿ) ⟶ 𝓙ⁿ`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.epi_pullbackIdealPow` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.exists_epi_pullback_idealPow`: **the morphism
  `h^*(Iⁿ) ⟶ (h⁻¹I)ⁿ` is an epimorphism.**
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPullback.epi_externalTensorIdealPowMul`: **the morphism
  `pr₁^*(𝓘ⁿ) ⊗ pr₂^*(𝓘'ⁿ) ⟶ 𝓙ⁿ` is an epimorphism.**

## Implementation notes

`PresheafOfModules.pullback` is defined as the left adjoint of the pushforward, so there is no
description of the sections of `h^*(Iⁿ)` to work with. Both halves of the argument therefore go
through the adjunction rather than through sections of the pullback: a morphism out of
`h^*(Iⁿ)` is a morphism `Iⁿ ⟶ h_*((h⁻¹I)ⁿ)`, whose sections are computable, and the unit of the
adjunction provides sections of `h^*(Iⁿ)` whose images are known.

The two spellings `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` and `SheafOfModules X.ringCatSheaf` of the
same category agree definitionally but not under the reduced transparency at which `rw` and
instance search operate; the section computations are therefore assembled as terms and the
epimorphism is transported from `SheafOfModules` by the cancellation property.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FZ0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FZ0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CA)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
